No, the entire point of the Macedonian phalanx was to use _massed_
shields and pikes. That game really doesn't work when you're on your
own. You just don't have the mobility you need. In a phalanx, you don't
need that mobility, because you're protected by your colleagues on at
least three sides. All you have to do is point all pikes in the right
direction and move forward, and something will inevitably get impaled on
them sooned or later. If you're running around all alone in a dungeon,
you do want to be able to stick your pike exactly where you want it. You
can't do that with a shield, and you can't do that with the a pike of
Epameinondaic size, either.

